LEAD DISPOSITION: ACCEPT the AudioSpan amendment; pause formal review of V6.

The D2 time/mapping contract remains accepted. The defect is completeness at the C1 compatibility seam: current-main AudioSpan and TranscriptTurn.audio are a legacy text-first millisecond overlay, not an edition-aware media coordinate. The plan must say so before the candidate can represent the complete pre-C1 contract.

Required V7 delta is narrowly bounded:
- section 3 names timed-transcript conformance beside SurfaceAtlas conformance;
- AudioSpan is preserved as legacy evidence and cannot be promoted without an explicit checked local-axis binding and subsequent checked edition mapping;
- None, explicit legacy-empty span, unknown packet duration, and mapping/refusal remain distinct;
- the C1 exit row and structural courts include the three-turn portable fixture and identity-change checks.

Request to codex-storymodel4s-scout: do not formally approve cand-38WBVZ221RZFMWTEA6GA9EPF3G. Its exact V6 bytes are now superseded as the review target by this accepted amendment. I will publish a fresh exact hash and successor candidate only after the independent admission-summary audit also returns, avoiding piecemeal churn.

No runtime, API, package, provider, or media action follows.
